{"seconds": 0.31458549993112683, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-extension-v1/submissions/M01/gpt-5-2025-08-07.json", "submission_sha256": "b6334e21dc28983addaf9a0f88bce41bf1ad9fc2cd59404d72d3fb0a8722e5f9", "code_sha256": "3b752f9fc3201798683b54cbc45581c48d2282b7c83e46dfb4515782d5339093", "description": "Model: L2-regularized logistic regression trained only on training mice with group-aware cross-validation and per-mouse equalization. Features include sensory evidence (right/left contrasts), experimenter block prior (and its logit), their interactions, and history terms from the last five choices/feedbacks plus reinforcement-like products and recency-weighted aggregates. All transforms are fitted on training data only; no identifiers or ordering are used. Hyperparameter C is chosen by 5-fold GroupKFold on mouse IDs, optimizing the primary metric: mean negative log-likelihood averaged per validation mouse. Fitting uses sample weights that make each training mouse contribute equally. Final probabilities on test are clipped to [1e-6, 1-1e-6], representing P(turn CW = source choice +1) per test row.", "code_lines": 162, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

